# SYNTHETIC fixture. Not a captured sweep.
# Hand-built because no endpoint in this project's registry has ever
# answered the classes query with a parsed, empty result: every captured
# sweep records sw:metric:classes as "verified" or "indeterminate", so a
# dqv:value "absent" for that metric cannot be captured live today. The
# shape is the same as any other measured run; only the verdict differs.
#
# Why "absent" needs a fixture of its own. It is one of the two ASSERTIVE
# verdicts in the closed vocabulary: prober/src/resolve.rs records it for a
# SelectIris probe only when the endpoint answered with a parsed SPARQL-JSON
# result that bound nothing, which is evidence the endpoint holds no
# classes rather than an absence of evidence. The prober writes no
# sw:ContentSample beside it (it skips a sample that bound no values), so
# this run measures the metric and publishes no sample, and the page must
# say that the probe established the negative instead of saying, as it
# would for "indeterminate", that nothing was established.
#
# 16 quads, one run graph (urn:sparqlwatch:run:2026-08-22T20:00:00Z), one
# endpoint, two dqv:QualityMeasurement facts and no sw:ContentSample.
